icle information</h4><p><strong>Source</strong><br/><a href="/euclid.jdg">J. Differential Geom.</a>,  Volume 11, Number 4 (1976), 573-598.</p><p><strong>Dates</strong><br/>First available in Project Euclid:  25 June 2008<br/></p><p><strong>Permanent link to this document</strong><br/>https://projecteuclid.org/euclid.jdg/1214433725</p><p><strong>Digital Object Identifier</strong><br/>doi:10.4310/jdg/1214433725</p><p><strong>Mathematical Reviews number (MathSciNet)</strong><br/><a href="https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=0448404"> MR0448404</a><br/></p><p><strong>Zentralblatt MATH identifier</strong><br/><a href="https://zbmath.org/?q=an:0371.46011">0371.46011</a></p><p class="subjects"><strong>Subjects</strong><br/> Primary: <a title="Search this subject in Euclid" href="/search_result?type=index&amp;linkedSearch=1&amp;q.a.subject=58D15">58D15: Manifolds of mappings [See also 46T10, 54C35]</a><br/> Secondary: <a title="Search this subject in Euclid" href="/search_result?type=index&amp;linkedSearch=1&amp;q.a.subject=46E35">46E35: Sobolev spaces and other spaces of "smooth" functions, embedding theorems, trace theorems</a> <a title="Search this subject in Euclid" href="/search_result?type=index&amp;linkedSearch=1&amp;q.a.subject=53C20">53C20: Global Riemannian geometry, including pinching [See also 31C12, 58B20]</a></p><h4>Citation</h4><div id="printer-citation"><p><span id="dynamic_citation">Aubin, Thierry. Probl&#xE8;mes isop&#xE9;rim&#xE9;triques et espaces de Sobolev. 
